# Discriminant test: sentences with many readings, to see how the discriminant choices needed
# to reach one reading scale with the number of readings. Built from the lilt-bank's vocabulary
# (stacked relatives, negation, quantified datives, conditionals). Reading counts with the
# lilt-bank rules (main_lfgxdrt_inference_grammar), 2026-11-05.

# 7 readings
The chef who cooked the soup that every guest praised received a prize.

# 14 readings
No student who read the article that a professor wrote failed every exam.

# 20 readings
The librarian lent every student who visited the library a book that Sue recommended.

# 32 readings
If every student who wrote a paper won a prize, the teacher did not give a student a book.

# 42 readings
Every student who read a book that Sue recommended did not pass an exam.

# 54 readings
The teacher did not give every student a book that Sue recommended.

# 69 readings
A professor who did not win a prize gave every student a book.

# 90 readings
The museum did not offer every artist who painted a portrait a contract.

# 100 readings
Every student in the class admires a professor who did not give a student an exam.

# 135 readings
The teacher did not give every student who wrote a paper a book that Sue recommended.
